Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(intake): add B2 review queue at /intake-review

Daily reception workflow for staged questionnaires. Each entry shows the
submission beside its candidate patients with differing fields highlighted,
and resolves in one click: Slucit / Vytvorit noveho / Zamitnout.

- Gated behind RequireAdmin. isAdminRole already accepts Owner and
  Administrator alongside the frontend's own role names, so the backend's
  Owner/Administrator/Staff model and the frontend's six-role clinical
  model meet correctly at this guard. Merging two patient records is
  irreversible in practice, so Staff must not reach the resolve actions.

- Every resolve call carries the intake fingerprint and the candidate
  revision the reviewer actually saw. A 409 means the data moved underneath
  them; the queue reloads and says so in plain Czech rather than silently
  applying a decision made against stale information.

- Field values arrive already masked for the viewer's role, so the client
  never decides what a Staff user may see. Sensitive fields carry a marker
  explaining the masking rather than looking like missing data.

- Rejection asks for a reason and requires 3+ characters. It is the one
  action that discards a patient's submission, and the audit entry needs a
  'why' that is still readable a year later.

Consumes the outcome shape defined by PatientIntakeMatchScorer, so the two
sides already agree. The endpoints it calls
(GET/POST /api/patients/intake-review) do not exist yet.

Typecheck: 0 errors in new files; repo total unchanged at 581.

